cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or dataset, please cite it as below, together with the
  article: P. Baratella, Phys. Rev. D 114, 063510 (2026), doi:10.1103/q5ld-kg6w.
type: software
title: "Supercooling exit from charge supersaturation: code and dataset"
version: 2.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Baratella
    given-names: Pietro
    affiliation: "Jožef Stefan Institute, Ljubljana"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7891-8933"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and dataset for the exit temperature of cosmological supercooling
  driven by charge supersaturation, in the model of Phys. Rev. D 114, 063510
  (2026), doi:10.1103/q5ld-kg6w, arXiv:2512.16601. The dataset, a
  CF-conventions NetCDF file, gives the first temperature at which the
  condensation condition is met across the model's parameter space, together
  with the two edges of its domain and a quality-control flag; a test suite
  validates it against exact identities. The code is released under the MIT
  licence, the dataset data/supercooling_exit.nc under CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - cosmological phase transitions
  - supercooling
  - thermal field theory
  - NetCDF
  - dataset
